-- title:
--   Descent of node coordinates from the crossing-model completion
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\pi \in W$ generate that maximal ideal, and let $w \ge 1$ be a natural number. Let $O$ be a noetherian commutative local ring and write $\widehat{O}$ for the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal. Assume given a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from $\widehat{O}$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ w)`, equal to $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi^w)$ (formal power series in two variables over $W$ modulo the ideal generated by $X_0X_1$ minus the constant series $\pi^w$), and an element $t \in O$ whose image in $\widehat{O}$ is carried by $\iota$ to `const (π ^ w) π`, the class of the constant power series $\pi$. Assume further that the node is already split over $O$: there are two distinct prime ideals $\mathfrak p_1 \neq \mathfrak p_2$ of $O$, both containing $t$ and both different from the maximal ideal of $O$. The conclusion is that there exist $x_n, y_n, u \in O$ and elements $\gamma, \gamma'$ of the crossing model such that $u$, $\gamma$ and $\gamma'$ are units, the image of $x_n$ in $\widehat{O}$ satisfies $\iota(x_n) = \gamma \cdot U(\pi^w)$ and that of $y_n$ satisfies $\iota(y_n) = \gamma' \cdot V(\pi^w)$, where $U(\pi^w)$ and $V(\pi^w)$ are the two coordinate elements of the model, together with $x_n y_n = t^w u$ in $O$ and $\mathfrak m_O = (x_n, y_n, t)$.
--
--   This is the Zariski-level descent step for a node: local coordinates cutting out the two branches, known after completion from the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^w)$, are produced already in the noetherian local ring $O$ itself, together with the relation $x_n y_n = t^w u$ and the presentation of the maximal ideal. It feeds the construction of node coordinates on a curve and the per-node analysis of the modular curves of full level used in the Diamond-style arguments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_mul_eq_pow_mul_and_maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_pow.lean

